 AWS for DevOps – Real-World Architecture Case Studies

These aren’t theory questions. These test how you think 👇

🔹 Case 1: High-Traffic Web Application
 • How would you design a highly available web application on AWS?
 • Which services would you choose for compute, load balancing, and database?
 • How would you handle sudden traffic spikes?
 • How would you design for zero downtime deployments?

🔹 Case 2: Multi-Region Disaster Recovery
 • How would you design DR for a business-critical application?
 • Which DR strategy would you choose and why?
 • How would you route traffic during a regional failure?
 • How would you test this setup?

🔹 Case 3: Secure CI/CD Platform
 • How would you design a secure CI/CD pipeline on AWS?
 • How would you manage secrets and credentials?
 • How would you prevent insecure code or infrastructure from reaching production?
 • How would you audit pipeline activity?

🔹 Case 4: Cost-Optimized Architecture
 • How would you design an architecture optimized for cost?
 • Where would you use Spot Instances or serverless?
 • How would you track and control cost continuously?
 • What trade-offs would you accept?

🔹 Case 5: Containerized Microservices
 • How would you design a microservices platform on AWS?
 • Would you choose ECS or EKS and why?
 • How would services communicate securely?
 • How would you handle logging and monitoring?

🔹 Case 6: Data-Intensive Application
 • How would you design for high read/write throughput?
 • Which database services would you choose?
 • How would you handle backups and scaling?
 • How would you ensure data consistency?

🔹 Case 7: Enterprise Multi-Account Setup
 • How would you design a multi-account AWS environment?
 • How would you enforce security guardrails?
 • How would you centralize logging and monitoring?
 • How would you manage cross-account access?

🔹 Case 8: Incident Scenario
 • A production outage is reported — what is your first step?
 • How do you identify root cause under pressure?
 • How do you communicate during the outage?
 • What changes would you make after recovery?

💡 Architecture interviews don’t test memory — they test judgment.
